<title>UK: Electrophoretics up on CJD test news.</title>
<headline>Electrophoretics up on CJD test news.</headline>
<dateline>LONDON 1996-09-27</dateline>
<text>
<p>Shares in biotechnology minnow Electrophoretics International Plc leapt on Friday after the company said late yesterday it had acquired a licence to develop a test for Creutzfeldt-Jacob Disease (CJD).</p>
<p>The stock was marked 20p higher at 85.</p>
<p>In a statement after the London market closed on Thursday, the company said it acquired a license from the U.S. National Insitute of Health to commercialise a diagnostic test for CJD.</p>
<p>It said it was working to make the test commercially available as soon as possible.</p>
<p>-- London Newsroom +44 171 542 5106</p>
